/-!
# `fd_r43x6_mul_fast` computes `mulFastResult`

The main theorem of this file: denoting the lifted SLLVM program
`fd_r43x6_mul_fast` produces exactly the lane expression `mulFastResult x y` --
the fully expanded `za + (zb <<< 7) + zb * 24` of the source's final fold
(LLVM turned `(zb <<< 4) + (zb <<< 3)` into `zb * 24`), stated in terms of the
`vpmadd52` lane functions `mulLo52`/`mulHi52`.

Intermediates carry the variable names from `fd_r43x6.h` (`x0`-`x5` broadcasts
as `xb0`-`xb5`, `t0`-`t6`, `p1j`-`p6j`/`q3j`-`q6j`, `zl`/`zh`, `za`/`zb`).

Note that in the valuation, `%arg0` (= `x`) is the *second* component of
`Ctxt.Valuation.ofPair` and `%arg1` (= `y`) the first: `ofPair` builds the
context `[t₁, t₂]` with `%arg1` as variable 0.
-/

